(contestants laughing)

00:08:21.395 --> 00:08:22.280
- Not at all.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:24.150
- I thought Steven was like seven-five.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:24.983
I'm not gonna lie.

00:08:24.983 --> 00:08:25.816
- Dude, I thought you were taller than me.

00:08:25.816 --> 00:08:26.649
(laughs)

00:08:26.649 --> 00:08:27.482
- [Steven] I was like trying to-

00:08:27.482 --> 00:08:31.290
- I was gonna say, I don't
think we got it wrong.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.925
- [Male Crew] In spot
number six, we have Laila,

00:08:33.925 --> 00:08:35.736
at 97 pounds.

00:08:35.736 --> 00:08:37.308
- Oh wow!

00:08:37.308 --> 00:08:41.980
- [Male Crew] In spot number
five, we have Carmen, at 138.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:46.123
In spot number four,
we have Ruben, at 175.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:51.499
In spot number three,
we have Steven, at 220.

00:08:51.499 --> 00:08:55.630
In spot number two, we
have Sabrina, at 309.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.998
And in spot number one,
we have Richard, at 315.

00:08:58.998 --> 00:08:59.931
- We got it right.
- Yep, we did.

00:08:59.931 --> 00:09:01.000
- [Announcer] You win!

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.032
- I never doubted you guys.

00:09:02.032 --> 00:09:03.100
(contestants laughing)

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.530
- So, I guess I can reveal this now.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.194
So I actually in the past four
years, I've lost 150 pounds.

00:09:07.194 --> 00:09:08.027
- [Group] Oh wow!

00:09:08.027 --> 00:09:09.770
- I actually used to be 441.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.500
So I feel a lot better about myself.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.450
And I focus on it every day.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.080
- Mine is a big part of my life now,

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:16.107
'cause I want kids and stuff.

00:09:16.107 --> 00:09:18.780
And you have to be healthy to do so.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:19.870
In general, how I look,

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.380
like I went to Mexico

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:23.007
and even my friends were asking,

00:09:23.007 --> 00:09:24.410
"Why aren't you posting any pictures?"

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.243
And I'm like,

00:09:25.243 --> 00:09:26.737
"girl, cause they ugly!"

00:09:26.737 --> 00:09:29.130
I didn't like how any of the
pictures were coming out.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.790
So I literally came home from
Mexico and called the doctor

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:33.623
and was like,

00:09:33.623 --> 00:09:34.697
"Can I on the program?"

00:09:34.697 --> 00:09:35.660
So.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:36.493
- You're not ugly.

00:09:36.493 --> 00:09:37.326
Sorry to say that.

00:09:37.326 --> 00:09:38.837
- [Richard] I was gonna
say like, nah, you, nah.

00:09:38.837 --> 00:09:39.952
- [Steven] You're not ugly.

00:09:39.952 --> 00:09:41.620
- Thanks guys.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:43.680
- I don't know why you
wouldn't wanna post pictures.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.513
You're beautiful.

00:09:44.513 --> 00:09:45.650
I'm not saying like,

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:48.130
because you are trying to lose weight,

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:49.660
that inherently makes,

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.304
that shouldn't make you
dislike the pictures.

00:09:51.304 --> 00:09:52.137
- [Group] Yeah.

00:09:52.137 --> 00:09:53.903
- I think you're beautiful regardless,

00:09:53.903 --> 00:09:56.670
but you can do exactly what
you wanna do with your body.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:57.503
You know what I mean?

00:09:57.503 --> 00:10:00.120
- Well yeah. I used to weigh 450 pounds.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:01.210
- Oh wow.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.043
- Yeah.

00:10:02.043 --> 00:10:04.300
I've been big my whole life.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:06.687
The food addiction thing was what got me.

00:10:06.687 --> 00:10:07.960
And I spoke about that.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.070
Very, very real.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:10.530
Went sober three years ago.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:12.170
Got the bariatric two and a half.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:16.028
Quitting food was harder
than quitting alcohol.

00:10:16.028 --> 00:10:17.884
And that shook me.

00:10:17.884 --> 00:10:20.570
It's just as easy as
saying I snapped my leg,

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.139
I needed to be surgically fixed.

00:10:22.139 --> 00:10:25.770
I was at a point where my mind
and my body were so broken,

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:27.667
I needed it to be fixed.

00:10:27.667 --> 00:10:29.560
And I got that reset button.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.700
And the misconception that I hate

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.170
is that it's the easy way out.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:36.730
But they don't see the hard mental process

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.020
in what I'm going through now,

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.620
to fix the identity issues
I was working through

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:41.453
and all this stuff.

00:10:41.453 --> 00:10:42.900
There's a lot of me
still broken from that.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.340
I just wanna say to you,

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:46.300
I feel you were pushing
yourself down there.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.530
Now that, and you too.

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:50.589
Now that I'm here, I realize I wasn't bad.

00:10:50.589 --> 00:10:52.500
(beep)

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.980
I realized I wasn't that
bad when I was there.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:55.813
You know?

00:10:55.813 --> 00:10:57.100
So like, don't think you guys are

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.230
in the right (beep) right now, right?

00:10:58.230 --> 00:10:59.410
Like this is the beautiful part.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:03.790
And I think my view of body positivity is

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:05.020
pretty (beep) up.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.530
- Because when I was
trying to lose weight,

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:09.580
I had everyone here in LA
saying, nah, you're beautiful.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:10.660
Don't.

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:12.020
And I'm like, nah, I'm unhealthy.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:12.853
Right?

00:11:12.853 --> 00:11:13.686
Like I'm dying.

00:11:13.686 --> 00:11:14.958
Like, you know, it's not about my beauty.

00:11:14.958 --> 00:11:15.791
- [Richard] Right, right, right.

00:11:15.791 --> 00:11:18.840
- Being the lightest one here,

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.950
I'm like anemic, borderline pre-diabetic.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:27.010
I have a lot of issues just
because of my lifestyle.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:29.960
But you know, I can't
necessarily carry the weight.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:30.910
- Just cause I worked out a lot,

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:31.980
'cause I did a lot of sports,

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.210
I was always so thin.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.910
And when I stopped, so people would like,

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:37.010
they always assumed I had like anorexia.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.070
All this like different stuff.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:38.903
And I was fine.

00:11:38.903 --> 00:11:39.736
I was eating fine.

00:11:39.736 --> 00:11:41.510
And then when they stopped
making the comments,

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.238
I thought that I had
like blown up basically.

00:11:44.238 --> 00:11:46.870
And then I developed the body dysmorphia.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.240
And then I was having eating disorders.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.740
And when I lost weight doing that,

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:51.840
people would compliment me.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:55.360
And that's where they
equate size to health.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.080
And I was losing hair and
the least healthy I ever was.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:59.230
But, since I was small,

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.063
they were like,

00:12:00.063 --> 00:12:00.896
"Oh, like you're healthy."

00:12:00.896 --> 00:12:02.040
- It's definitely important you guys.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.620
Find yourself because as a big guy

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.560
I attributed my identity to my size.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:06.393
- [Richard] Right.
- [Sabrina] Yeah.

00:12:06.393 --> 00:12:09.010
- And now I'm stuck in therapy
trying to find out who I am.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:09.843
Right.

00:12:09.843 --> 00:12:12.060
Because I was Big Steve forever.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.470
- My whole life I've been Big Rich,

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:14.303
you know what I'm saying?

00:12:14.303 --> 00:12:15.690
And I have body dysmorphia.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.770
Well, I still see the
dude that was 450 pounds

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:18.603
in the mirror.

00:12:18.603 --> 00:12:19.759
People think that when you lose weight

00:12:19.759 --> 00:12:21.060
the battle's over.

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.420
But there's a whole mental thing

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.590
that you're supposed to address as well.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.040
And if you're struggling with weight,

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.850
whether you wanna get big or get small,

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.400
just understand there's
a mental aspect to it.

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.430
And you want to address that as well.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:31.660
And at the end of the day

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.700
love yourself, you know, be healthy.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:36.996
But there's more to it than
just the physical, I would say.

00:12:36.996 --> 00:12:39.663
(calming music)

